11.what is the evolutionary singnificance of Genomic sequencing in ecology with example 5 mark\par

\pard\widctlpar\sl360\slmult1\qj\cf0\f7  \b0\f8\par
Whole-genome analysis of organisms at crucial or disputed positions in the tree of life can be\par
expected to contribute significantly to our knowledge of evolution.\par
\f9\bullet\f10  \f8 The sea squirt, \b\f11 ci. Intestinalis \b0\f8 was chosen as a model because it belongs to a group, the\par
Urochordata, with properties similar to the ancestors of vertebrates.\par
\f9\bullet\f10  \f8 The study of this species should provide valuable information about the early evolution of the\par
phylum to which we belong ourselves. Many other organisms, although not on the list for a\par
genome project to date, have a strong case for being declared as model species for\par
evolutionary arguments. These include the velvet worm, Peripatus, traditionally seen as a\par
missing link between the arthropods and annelids, but now classified as a separate phylum in\par
the panarthropoda lineage, and the springtail, folsomia candida, formerly regarded as a\par
primitive insect, but now sug-gested to have developed the hexapod bodyplan before the\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sl360\slmult1\qj insects separated from the crustaceans.\cf4\b\f0\par

