\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qj For a population in\~Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium in a situation where there are only two alleles at a particular locus, p + q = 1.0. The frequency of genotypes in a population in Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium can be calculated as (p + q)\super 2\nosupersub\~= (p + q) x (p + q) = p\super 2\nosupersub\~+ 2pq + q\super 2\nosupersub\~= 1.0. \par
The conditions necessary to maintain\~constent\~allele frequencies in a population are: \par

