\f15 (3)\tab\f0\lang2057 large population size,\lang1033\par
\f15 (4)\tab\f0\lang2057 no immigration, and \lang1033\par
\f15 (5)\tab\f0\lang2057 equal survival and reproductive rates for all genotypes. \lang1033\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa200\sl240\slmult1\lang2057 When a population is not in Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium, the Hardy-Weinberg principle helps us to identify the evolutionary forces that may be in play. \par

